      "side": 1,
      "message": "This assumes that WP_L will have its default value at the start of this test, but if the tests are shuffled, that might not be true. I suspect that if you do something like\n```\n# Enable test shuffling\nZTEST_SHUFFLE\u003dy\n# Run every suite 2 times\nZTEST_SHUFFLE_SUITE_REPEAT_COUNT\u003d2\n# Run every test 3 times per suite\nZTEST_SHUFFLE_TEST_REPEAT_COUNT\u003d3\n```\nin your prj.conf, you will find that this test fails at least once.\n\nI would suggest\n1. putting the WP-asserted and WP-deasserted tests into separate suites, and\n1. providing separate `_before` functions for each suite to set WP to the appropriate value explicitly.",
      "revId": "1fd0b484ee40c61701641d56059dfc64c57afade",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
